 "_comment": "Composed, not recorded: a forecast for Accra, the capital of Ghana (the city centre, rounded to 0.1 degree), with plausible weather for mid-November, in degrees Celsius and WMO weather codes. Accra keeps UTC all year, the emulated bar's zone out of the box, so the forecast's hours line up with the bar's clock. It stands in for what GET https://apps-api.busy.app/weather/v1/forecast answers a bar that asks with its device key and without coordinates: the API then places the bar by its address and says \"source\": \"geoip\". The shape (the fields, their types and units, 24 hours and 7 days) is that of the answer a bar on firmware 1.3.1 got on 2026-11-09; none of its place or numbers is kept. packages/server/device-key.mjs answers such requests from this, with the times moved to now (EMU-244).",
